  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nUpper level low pressure will dive southeast across the Lower Great \nLakes region tonight through Saturday. At the surface, a cold front \nhas swept east across the local forecast area this morning leaving \ngusty northwest flow in its wake. Anticipate for a period of \nscattered lake effect rain showers to continue across the \ntraditional snowbelt through Saturday night. Lake effect showers \nwill briefly exit Saturday night into Sunday morning as a ridge of \nhigh pressure builds overhead from the southwest. Another upper \nlevel shortwave will dive southeast across the eastern Great Lakes \nSunday into Monday with lake effect showers downwind of Lake\nErie in Northeast Ohio and Northwest Pennsylvania. \nAdditionally, it will remain gusty through the weekend with \nnorthwesterly winds gusting to 25-30 MPH on Saturday and \nsouthwesterly to westerly winds gusting up to 35 MPH on Sunday.\n\nRemaining cooler this weekend with low temperatures tonight through \nSunday falling into the low to mid 30s. High temperatures in the \nupper 40s to lower 50s on Saturday will warm into the mid to upper \n50s by Sunday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nThe first half of next week looks mainly dry and mild as surface \nhigh pressure remains across the Ohio Valley. Another upper trough \nwill dig south into the region later in the week. However, current \nmedium range models have some differences in exact timing. For now, \nexpect for unsettled weather to return at some point later next \nweek.",
